-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Voyager backend (Bioqore)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Sources:
  - github.com/Bioqore/voyager-flask-back-end (commit e4f4ef7, 2026-07-02)
    Flask API, pydantic request validators (validators/schemas.py), tests.
  - github.com/Bioqore/py-common (commit b77092c, 2026-07-31)
    PostgreSQL data model and queries (VoyagerDatabaseManagement.py,
    DatabaseManagement.py), structured logging and request correlation
    (Logging.py, Middleware.py).

Authors (from the repositories' history): Tim (timbioqore, tlorgeree),
Kai Suematsu (ks-bio), Anh.

Permission: the owner of these repositories authorized porting them into Kalos,
including the backend setup, on 2026-11-20 ("port everything"). Neither
repository carried a license file; they are used here under that permission and
under the terms below.

What was adapted (re-implemented in Kalos's architecture, not copied):
  - the project / factor / experiment-link / outcome data model, as
    kalos/records/, kalos/storage/records_repo.py, kalos/storage/migrations/v9.py
    and kalos/api/routers/{projects,lineage,units}.py (docs/RECORDS.md);
  - the recursive experiment-lineage traversal, as a bounded traversal in
    kalos/records/lineage.py;
  - the data-unit table, as the code registry kalos/normalize/unit_registry.py;
  - the request-validation pattern (strings trimmed, every field described), as
    kalos/api/schemas/records.py;
  - the correlation-id logging, as kalos/api/request_context.py;
  - the PostgreSQL deployment and its CI service container, as the optional
    PostgreSQL backend (kalos/storage/backend.py,
    kalos/storage/migrations/pg_runner.py) and the CI postgres job.
Not adapted, by decision (see docs/RECORDS.md, "Not ported"): Google ID-token
login and HS256 token signing, the DISABLE_AUTH bypass, unauthenticated write
routes, the employee and customer tables, and per-environment .env files.

